#|
Linux/Android: create native output channels absent from an ordinary mouse.
The physical device only needs vertical/horizontal wheel input.

- Main wheel generates REL_Z; thumb wheel generates REL_RZ.
- Both also contribute to REL_DIAL (one input may feed multiple outputs).
- One notch generates 30 counts on each selected output.
- X/Y pointer movement is passed through; ordinary scrolling is suppressed.

A direct-input consumer must understand these extra output channels. They do
not turn the desktop cursor into a 3D cursor. This example demonstrates output
capabilities independent of the physical input device's advertised axes.
|#

(defcfg
  process-unmapped-keys no
  mouse-axis-map (
    (z (v 0.25))
    (rz (h 0.25))
    (dial (v 0.25) (h 0.25))
    (v)
    (h)
  )
)
(defsrc)
(deflayer base)
